.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Carl Runge&#x27;s 1901 example f(x) = 1/(1+25x^2) is smooth on [-1, 1], yet interpolating it at more equally spaced nodes makes the fit worse: oscillations near the endpoints grow without bound as the degree increases. This script shows the overshoot for growing degree, the maximum error blowing up, and the exponentially growing Lebesgue constant of equally spaced nodes that causes it.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/numerical_analysis/chebyshev/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_runge_phenomenon_thumb.png
